{# The data-table section, shared by every engine template that feeds the #}
{# data table findings. Parameterized by (findings list, heading text) so #}
{# each template passes its own heading text. The body is verbatim-pinned by #}
{# the section suite in src/lib.rs — wording or formatting drift fails CI. #}
{% macro data_tables_section(findings, heading) %}
{% if !findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

The defined data objects this function indexes that static analysis has
recognized as constant data tables — objects whose bytes decode coherently
at one element width and that nothing in the program writes. Where a
finding is credible, render each lookup of one of these objects as a named
`const` array of the element type and entry count shown, indexed where the
original offsets the object — do not re-scatter the decoded entries as
match arms or magic numbers:

{% for table in findings %}
- **{{ table.name }}**: `const [{{ table.element_type }}; {{ table.count }}]` (confidence {{ table.confidence }})
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
